 "notes": [
  "pyretechnics stores Anderson models 4, 5 and 10 live load in the herbaceous slot (live herbaceous moisture is then used); BehavePlus/GTR-371 treat it as live woody.",
  "pyretechnics FM7 live SAV 1550 vs 1500 in GTR-371 Table 8.",
  "pyretechnics loads are rounded to 4 decimals of lb/ft2.",
  "pyretechnics' 'behave' L/W option uses Anderson (1983) coefficients for m/s with a wind in mi/h; we compare with the 'rothermel' option (1 + 0.25 UE), which is BehavePlus's documented relation.",
  "Wind-on-slope cases differ by design and are reported separately: pyretechnics projects the horizontal wind and the slope onto the slope-tangential plane (a horizontal wind gains magnitude 1/cos(slope) in that plane and ROS is a slope-plane distance); FireSim follows BehavePlus (Rothermel wind factor from the given midflame wind, horizontal vector addition of wind and slope effects). Flat and slope-only cases test the same equations."
 ],
